SGINet client
=============

SGINet is a client for Silicon Graphics MIPS computers running IRIX.
It registers your SGI on https://sginet.flexion.io, shares its hinv
data and online status, and lets you browse other users machines,
take screenshots, search software packages, read the sgi.sh forum, 
post in the shoutbox and more.

This package installs:

  /usr/bin/sginet                 command line client (ncurses UI)
  /usr/bin/xsginet                X11/Motif client (subsystem x11)
  /usr/bin/xsginet-globe          OpenGL globe of SGINet machines
                                  (subsystem globe)
  /etc/init.d/sginet-daemon       online status daemon (init script)


1. Register your machine
------------------------

Before you use the X11 clients, register your SGI with the command
line client. Open a terminal and run:

  sginet

On first launch you will be asked to register your SGI computer.

If sginet complains about the terminal, try:  setenv TERM iris-ansi
(sh/ksh:  TERM=iris-ansi; export TERM)

Emulators: SGINet is intended for real SGI/MIPS hardware. Please 
do not register emulators. The cloud API silently rejects requests 
from emulators. 


2. Start xsginet
----------------

Run xsginet only after registration with sginet is complete:

  xsginet

The globe viewer can be opened from the xsginet menu
(Actions > View globe..) or started directly with:

  xsginet-globe

Unregistered, the globe is read-only. Register first to submit
your machine's location.


3. sginet-daemon (optional)
---------------------------

The sginet-daemon service reports the online status of your machine
to the cloud every 12 minutes. It is enabled with chkconfig and starts 
at boot, but it is NOT started by the installation. 
After registering, start it as root with:

  /etc/init.d/sginet-daemon start

If you do not want your machine to report uptime, disable it with:

  chkconfig sginet-daemon off


